      "updated": 1789763250451,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WHO DECIDES WHAT\n\nThe models propose: they search, read, quote, and draft.\nThe code decides what is allowed: grades, dates, quotes, themes, and language are checked in plain rules anyone can read.\nPeople decide what matters: the Hub keeps, drops, and adds programs, and can change a grade, with every change written down.",
      "fontSize": 23,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "3cvPyYMrQCE1HCLG_l0if",
      "originalText": "WHO DECIDES WHAT\n\nThe models propose: they search, read, quote, and draft.\nThe code decides what is allowed: grades, dates, quotes, themes, and language are checked in plain rules anyone can read.\nPeople decide what matters: the Hub keeps, drops, and adds programs, and can change a grade, with every change written down.",
